os","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrtannus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrtannus/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrtannus","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web/commits/8cc33ddd6c80b9228b7f1e3c8c7df612aa54e204/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T22:31:01Z","email":"chrtannus@gmail.com","name":"Christian Lopes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T22:31:01Z","email":"chrtannus@gmail.com","name":"Christian Lopes"},"message":"Validate falsy filterWidgets values and reject inherited attribute names (#767)\n\nReview follow-ups on #770:\n\n- SubNetworkPanel found the aspect with `aspect[FILTER_ASPECT_TAG]`, a\n  truthiness check, so `\"filterWidgets\": null` (or false, 0, \"\") was\n  skipped and never reached parseFilterAspects'' warning. Move the lookup\n  into findFilterAspect (getFilterAspect.ts), which selects by own-key\n  presence and returns the raw value.\n- The attribute-name guard only rejected __proto__, constructor and\n  prototype. Any other Object.prototype member (toString, valueOf, ...)\n  also resolves on a table row that lacks the column, handing the filter\n  a function as a value. Reject every name `in Object.prototype`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"209a66fe43927f707eb1b858fd0d5c14186817e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web/git/trees/209a66fe43927f707eb1b858fd0d5c14186817e3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cytoscape/cytoscape-web/git/commits/8cc33ddd6c80b9228b7f1e3c8c7df612aa54e204","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/989686?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrtannus/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/c