:"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/renovate","id":29139614,"login":"renovate[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90MjkxMzk2MTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/767fc75ecafefdf834c006ee7878ebbcf6561e21/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T13:37:17Z","email":"29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"renovate[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T13:37:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deps): update opentelemetry packages (#5191)\n\n* fix(deps): update opentelemetry packages\n\n* fix(telemetry): adapt to OpenTelemetry 0.223 / 2.12\n\n- Regenerate the lockfile (Renovate failed to do it because of the\n  minimumReleaseAge gate) and dedupe @opentelemetry/* so the telemetry\n  tree resolves a single version of each package.\n- Bump @opentelemetry/instrumentation-pg to 0.75.0 (fixes\n  GHSA-qqmp-wf37-98f9 / CVE-2026-104872, supersedes #5190).\n- sdk-trace-base is now a shim over @opentelemetry/sdk-trace: load\n  Tracer from there and pass the new (scope, options) constructor\n  arguments, including span limits, id generator and a noop meter\n  provider.\n- Update tests to the stable semantic conventions now emitted by the\n  instrumentations (db.query.text, http.request.method, url.scheme,\n  url.path).\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n* chore: exclude OpenTelemetry 0.223 / 2.12 from minimumReleaseAge\n\npnpm verifies lockfile entries against minimumReleaseAge even on frozen\ninstalls, so CI fails until these releases are 24h old. Exclude the 32\nOpenTelemetry packages pulled in by this update.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","tree":{"sha":"1e2d3cf6b38bb81a2af28ea519c22ec4466609fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/trees/1e2d3cf6b38bb81a2af28ea519c22ec4466609fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/commits/767fc75ecafefdf834c006ee7878ebbcf6561e21","verification":{"payload":"tree 1e2d3cf6b38bb81a2af28ea519c22ec4466609fe\nparent 97691c2f2308389c193fd8f16a49b1e5308bb706\nauthor renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1791380237 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791380237 -0700\n\nfix(deps): update opentelemetry packages (#5191)\n\n* fix(deps): update opentelemetry packages\n\n* fix(telemetry): adapt to OpenTelemetry 0.223 / 2.12\n\n- Regenerate the lockfile (Renovate failed to do it because of the\n  minimumReleaseAge gate) and dedupe @opentelemetry/* so the telemetry\n  tree resolves a single version of each package.\n- Bump @opentelemetry/instrumentation-pg to 0.75.0 (fixes\n  GHSA-qqmp-wf37-98f9 / CVE-2026-104872, supersedes #5190).\n- sdk-trace-base is now a shim over @opentelemetry/sdk-trace: load\n  Tracer from there and pass the new (scope, options) constructor\n  arguments, including span limits, id generator and a noop meter\n  provider.\n- Update tests to the stable semantic conventions now emitted by the\n  instrumentations (db.query.text, http.request.method, url.scheme,\n  url.path).\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n* chore: exclude OpenTelemetry 0.223 / 2.12 from minimumReleaseAge\n\npnpm verifies lockfile entries against minimumReleaseAge even on frozen\ninstalls, so CI fails until these releases are 24h old. Exclude the 32\nOpenTelemetry packages pulled in by this update.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\nCo-authored-by: renovate[bot] <29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxksNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzxwQACkxCCspNnFTPE9hOVafnEDu\nLM1mQkV+DIhaZFmjG916cPbcNoXlON3Wc/cfG/MYkt5FpBD/OC+wSDOJGx/bemW6\n7tbydc4vKcuaNFyg2W8vy1RU3MGJdk1izywRWQHBzRMNqlwsXJBa05ZnTlAtZt3s\nle/nfMurT35AcBMrRJOkehDoms07LywigCyHn6Cxmjq90fG90bdq1S6mzsx5e4P3\nP8qHPUFSg9WAsjbre5cu2fQ4PSos9/wmF3XyGPuQsy9nNcAF1g2RVNhiTM0m3IYS\nRyTJFnplx4VBg3OK1Fppdu4SQDtx81OLo+Rnj7Tm2nD55Z0QXYKwUx6XzkGdAe6l\n9LCq352kzCTtkRLuw0DPrqbdPxnLfD13mGcz8bmNCGyBlSZysD/d+N+vcikomrUA\n3UTskgtn5MTpi02dW9bmBOSjj8gYfLhMuPvB/gdbMRddKyUCmf5TXOUo7U08nt14\nN8tcyRr/4tJY+tc5JJBo9obCZ6wvah4RhhUt3vKEDkt5OhNABsXJXGM3ZWxdK/ry\nc46DxJ9fwBME3HkplycJANogY6ECZE0SiDWII3AOmy9MO1wjwUjEwS/CLk1uyShn\nSnPIBSrtpqNuNepB3wQJH1+d6RKurji/j58GLayFXUw9SIlW5SDSm+B8e90Kpbde\nOzRSO01u4E5/r/Rq3EKO\n=o+TC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T13:37:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/platformatic/platformatic/commit/767fc75ecafefdf834c006ee7878ebbcf6561e21","node_id":"C_kwDOIC2I7NoAKDc2N2ZjNzVlY2FmZWZkZjgzNGMwMDZlZTc4NzhlYmJjZjY1NjFlMjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/platformatic/platformatic/commit/97691c2f2308389c193fd8f16a49b1e5308bb706","sha":"97691c2f2308389c193fd8f16a49b1e5308bb706","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/97691c2f2308389c193fd8f16a49b1e5308bb706"}],"sha":"767fc75ecafefdf834c006ee7878ebbcf6561e21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/767fc75ecafefdf834c006ee7878ebbcf6561e21"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/604220?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leorossi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leorossi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leorossi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leorossi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leorossi","id":604220,"login":"leorossi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNDIyMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leorossi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leorossi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leorossi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leorossi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leorossi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leorossi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/97691c2f2308389c193fd8f16a49b1e5308bb706/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T09:16:53Z","email":"leonardo.rossi@gmail.com","name":"Leonardo Rossi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T09:16:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gateway): count websocket links once in activeWsConnections (#5143)\n\n* fix(gateway): count websocket links once in activeWsConnections\n\nA proxied websocket link is torn down from both of its sockets, so\n@fastify/http-proxy can deliver onDisconnect more than once for the same\nconnection. The gauge decremented on every delivery, so it lost one per\nconnection: it reached zero while connections were still open, then kept\ngoing negative for the lifetime of the process.\n\nThe gauge counts links, not callbacks, so the source socket is now tracked in\na WeakSet and both hooks are idempotent. This holds regardless of how many\ntimes the underlying hook fires, which is the right place for the guard: the\ngauge is the thing that has to stay correct.\n\nThe existing test already walked 0 -> 1 -> 2 -> 1 -> 0, but could not catch\nthis. It read the gauge immediately after awaiting the first onDisconnect\nevent, while the duplicate was still in flight, and its \\d+ pattern could not\nmatch a negative sample — a drifted gauge simply failed the match and was\nreported as 0. It now settles before reading and accepts a sign.\n\nSigned-off-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Leonardo Rossi <leonardo.rossi@gmail.com>\n\n* chore(gateway): require @fastify/http-proxy >= 11.6.3\n\n11.6.3 is the first release carrying \"fix: call the onDisconnect hook once per\nconnection\", the upstream half of the previous commit: the hook is no longer\ndelivered twice when a proxied websocket link is torn down, so consumers of\nws.hooks.onDisconnect stop seeing duplicates too, not just our gauge.\n\nIt also carries \"fix: normalize encoded backslashes in proxy paths\", which is\nworth having in a proxy regardless.\n\nSigned-off-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Leonardo Rossi <leonardo.rossi@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Leonardo Rossi <leonardo.rossi@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"f0b4ff0f1b5e3fd0bab5d58c7a6752e5cbab866b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/trees/f0b4ff0f1b5e3fd0bab5d58c7a6752e5cbab866b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/commits/97691c2f2308389c193fd8f16a49b1e5308bb706","verification":{"payload":"tree f0b4ff0f1b5e3fd0bab5d58c7a6752e5cbab866b\nparent 66408100677db235c540b4ce62f20a8b96961497\nauthor Leonardo Rossi <leonardo.rossi@gmail.com> 1791364613 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791364613 -0700\n\nfix(gateway): count websocket links once in activeWsConnections (#5143)\n\n* fix(gateway): count websocket links once in activeWsConnections\n\nA proxied websocket link is torn down from both of its sockets, so\n@fastify/http-proxy can deliver onDisconnect more than once for the same\nconnection. The gauge decremented on every delivery, so it lost one per\nconnection: it reached zero while connections were still open, then kept\ngoing negative for the lifetime of the process.\n\nThe gauge counts links, not callbacks, so the source socket is now tracked in\na WeakSet and both hooks are idempotent. This holds regardless of how many\ntimes the underlying hook fires, which is the right place for the guard: the\ngauge is the thing that has to stay correct.\n\nThe existing test already walked 0 -> 1 -> 2 -> 1 -> 0, but could not catch\nthis. It read the gauge immediately after awaiting the first onDisconnect\nevent, while the duplicate was still in flight, and its \\d+ pattern could not\nmatch a negative sample — a drifted gauge simply failed the match and was\nreported as 0. It now settles before reading and accepts a sign.\n\nSigned-off-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Leonardo Rossi <leonardo.rossi@gmail.com>\n\n* chore(gateway): require @fastify/http-proxy >= 11.6.3\n\n11.6.3 is the first release carrying \"fix: call the onDisconnect hook once per\nconnection\", the upstream half of the previous commit: the hook is no longer\ndelivered twice when a proxied websocket link is torn down, so consumers of\nws.hooks.onDisconnect stop seeing duplicates too, not just our gauge.\n\nIt also carries \"fix: normalize encoded backslashes in proxy paths\", which is\nworth having in a proxy regardless.\n\nSigned-off-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Leonardo Rossi <leonardo.rossi@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Leonardo Rossi <leonardo.rossi@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxg4FCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANXEQABSG3qOaylOGEoDZZeMJ0e+7\nHAj5VyihsDlwNosqqJNVi654bYMuODPE2ii0V2ay9qKZS46DfhUdGxisqFZqzIyV\n2YNSUSzDTF8x2uc3BVB+0RLq01lyi9FX/1ZBVkG47NTlJiuugJPQjQfjyIOJWU4C\nOfswlITOI+OXqGoF0jS3waSfoNkDX1pVB/cozVugtcQeR6X3uizqncUc2m7PeW8D\npxXxj8UhByg/4xRL2egQqpMfcpnGHbIcBx/ahuDIKjm44IEbmfvyucyBOg4kf52t\ng2v8f4K72FZnkZQHkqPJSjja4hf6sIe9bR2W5F06SXFGasMd4jUOUC+NHNeOWvod\nu77R13h6YTwEKMvrmCJTQY6C9xft6y2/AOD1Kr2MkckBUt/AZQSd1y/rVo3sHU7K\n6ftU9brBOSLfKSpSPuebd9grQVtl3CEUvPtVnO8MSeW9HY1hr7pgVqQZtMmMw4eJ\nnKq0wMCzVphERGzA1OTagxmocXivEmLC/djLbrxKswohjhiQlOfZKeHtm+asrtyq\nplIZAIEZu2cbmPMlUhcut+uA1QkRBMIKEzc3IkvM4RWlU3tGZ07blRTxxF9BqfOT\nfXiv3WQGo0Rq6TkXAGxqAt5oe9HnjCbXZf28k1YYACnoMX+BChXiF4iPEMsJ/4B9\nNF3Dd+8swGQ6vfI+X8dQ\n=mbSh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T09:16:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","f