,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/afb3fdd23a6d5e22426bb80b9be8f5c15ddbe144"}],"sha":"1e4e775fc0ae6e2741f688c7deda1dac1595631a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/1e4e775fc0ae6e2741f688c7deda1dac1595631a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcollina","id":52195,"login":"mcollina","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/afb3fdd23a6d5e22426bb80b9be8f5c15ddbe144/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:25:23Z","email":"hello@matteocollina.com","name":"Matteo Collina"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:25:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(runtime): cover per-worker ports during worker replacement (#5160)\n\n* test(runtime): cover per-worker ports during worker replacement\n\nAdd a test that a worker replaced for a high ELU keeps its incremental\nport, and Linux-only tests (reusePort) that the per-worker ports never\nrefuse connections while an application restarts or a worker with a\nhigh ELU is replaced.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n* test(runtime): only fail the no-downtime tests on refused connections\n\nOn Linux the old worker resets its idle keep-alive sockets, and the\nconnections still queued on its listener unless net.ipv4.tcp_migrate_req\nis set, when it is replaced. Those show up as ECONNRESET while the port\nstays open, so assert on ECONNREFUSED only.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n* test(runtime): throttle the no-downtime poller and track unhealthy workers\n\nOn CI the worker replacing the busy one ended up replaced again. Throttle\nthe requests so the polling alone cannot push a worker over maxELU, and\nassert that only the busy worker becomes unhealthy, reporting which\nworkers did when the port check fails.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","tree":{"sha":"611383959b291871a9c16ab36a7d642be9793bc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/trees/611383959b291871a9c16ab36a7d642be9793bc5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/commits/afb3fdd23a6d5e22426bb80b9be8f5c15ddbe144","verification":{"payload":"tree 611383959b291871a9c16ab36a7d642be9793bc5\nparent 77b6c65fb750c17c0e30b24d2524e32cf0a53d4c\nauthor Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com> 1791300323 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791300323 -0700\n\ntest(runtime): cover per-worker ports during worker replacement (#5160)\n\n* test(runtime): cover per-worker ports during worker replacement\n\nAdd a test that a worker replaced for a high ELU keeps its incremental\nport, and Linux-only tests (reusePort) that the per-worker ports never\nrefuse connections while an application restarts or a worker with a\nhigh ELU is replaced.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n* test(runtime): only fail the no-downtime tests on refused connections\n\nOn Linux the old worker resets its idle keep-alive sockets, and the\nconnections still queued on its listener unless net.ipv4.tcp_migrate_req\nis set, when it is replaced. Those show up as ECONNRESET while the port\nstays open, so assert on ECONNREFUSED only.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n* test(runtime): throttle the no-downtime poller and track unhealthy workers\n\nOn CI the worker replacing the busy one ended up replaced again. Throttle\nthe requests so the polling alone cannot push a worker over maxELU, and\nassert that only the busy worker becomes unhealthy, reporting which\nworkers did when the port check fails.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxRLjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVRcQADkC2KUuiWLeYxMnFN3/Qh1O\njFaoZMbext+vSmPACSgjuDc/AIMYenZ3tEI3CQaZS7VWcIC6r27yxuIOS76jpR2C\nWNDWfsxtNMFZnU8k64f3eAj43ZPCh45xZxzA2jCJARjSc0m6HKT618sHfBwoEV92\nxUS4uPC2BlYkqWO6agpjbb3eOiW1kvzJkm4sV8SIeSfiAvCze6Iasnn1JD+KquFz\nUs+//754W6R/HhFsDl/7m/R9+JsMouto7saT96sJ/tpnsDNXVmnRT9FvsXuN/ZjC\nsMbYI+8+wsrMGEfRC+9Qszi1jjlVNhPDmeynXcODrTNchpqm6j1vHdyIZ9JWhxob\nURabJm5D6wsJH0447bdsknQYa7qWC/WyLogN4/eoOPBDRpQpOlcSOxctm2ioV3xe\nGgMw3gICvg14PfhRTLVt+Ss4RGk9K6dLTPQ1pcg1CCduTq4BR18tNoOGmigJSJMj\nd4GUiQrA1ZzjBVcslrdQ1KOYWIMYopOb4TAYGqPltRgLT1T3ZMO+MdxSNI6Bl56d\nJoLQGvGk0NQdxTGD7x/t8dqc4himHKIW7rQTxOSRKsD+dalydCEBpRI+SPZ3Zv7g\na2dxnmIFwCponx4IWPWaUKK7Rd6jSxqVD5i4qvsOYE2ZJMYpf/B/KHCkGw2t4Rsy\nNhiTS1WSL8twzr4Ul4is\n=Qh9I\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T15:25:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-f