AKDU0ODc3NTQ2YjUyOTQ5M2Y3ZWJjN2E5NjZhNDkyZWU5ZDcxNGEwNjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/platformatic/platformatic/commit/c39b1665eabde9442b65f4e4b52ad8f2e07fa56d","sha":"c39b1665eabde9442b65f4e4b52ad8f2e07fa56d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/c39b1665eabde9442b65f4e4b52ad8f2e07fa56d"}],"sha":"54877546b529493f7ebc7a966a492ee9d714a064","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/54877546b529493f7ebc7a966a492ee9d714a064"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcollina","id":52195,"login":"mcollina","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/c39b1665eabde9442b65f4e4b52ad8f2e07fa56d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T10:11:20Z","email":"hello@matteocollina.com","name":"Matteo Collina"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T10:11:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(runtime): flush the module compile cache once the boot is complete (#5114)\n\nNode.js only writes the module compile cache to disk when the process, or the\nworker thread that populated it, terminates. Applications are often killed\nabruptly (SIGKILL, OOM killer, container eviction), which discarded the whole\ncache accumulated while booting and made the next start pay the full\ncompilation cost again, including the very first boot of a fresh image, which\nis exactly the run that populates the cache.\n\nFlush it explicitly as soon as the boot is complete, when most modules have\nbeen loaded:\n\n- thread workers flush when the application controller emits `started`\n- applications running as a command flush when the child process reports its\n  URL, which is when their server is listening\n- the runtime process flushes when the runtime is started, which makes the\n  compile cache the CLI enables in `~/.cache/platformatic` durable as well\n\nThe flush is deferred so that it never delays the boot and repeated flushes\nare cheap, as Node.js skips the entries which have already been persisted.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Dx9tLmiQyM5x9KCpc5W2b3\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"76dff8a69b2e4c2357cdd15e5a9c83471a8c052c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/trees/76dff8a69b2e4c2357cdd15e5a9c83471a8c052c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/commits/c39b1665eabde9442b65f4e4b52ad8f2e07fa56d","verification":{"payload":"tree 76dff8a69b2e4c2357cdd15e5a9c83471a8c052c\nparent e52551284c86e1fab1b3465ca90adf9add4072d6\nauthor Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com> 1789553480 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789553480 -0700\n\nfix(runtime): flush the module compile cache once the boot is complete (#5114)\n\nNode.js only writes the module compile cache to disk when the process, or the\nworker thread that populated it, terminates. Applications are often killed\nabruptly (SIGKILL, OOM killer, container eviction), which discarded the whole\ncache accumulated while booting and made the next start pay the full\ncompilation cost again, including the very first boot of a fresh image, which\nis exactly the run that populates the cache.\n\nFlush it explicitly as soon as the boot is complete, when most modules have\nbeen loaded:\n\n- thread workers flush when the application controller emits `started`\n- applications running as a command flush when the child process reports its\n  URL, which is when their server is listening\n- the runtime process flushes when the runtime is started, which makes the\n  compile cache the CLI enables in `~/.cache/platformatic` durable as well\n\nThe flush is deferred so that it never delays the boot and repeated flushes\nare cheap, as Node.js skips the entries which have already been persisted.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Dx9tLmiQyM5x9KCpc5W2b3\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqmtICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2wQQAEbjAGpKbMwGohQ2xdnGDD8a\nnmjDGJvGMNChsy0akAujeiVghaCZUdOPR2CIH0t6HVqxTnJ5rzz+w0RNwAX4JvWd\nFjDFfpf/MTCGCWwKVVfnqq/x7+e47kIne1WkRjCN9wmU1S3hqeGas3pizsdP7vCr\nIZUui/lAgqs239dOBXaieB87Yc0KqD6c/+k4G81jVwOu4wd5dk2s2HpnDIdir24S\nisLFDIKUJEqqxhueHf+LEPG1TQq11RKRptrBCm7ZcnGNN8qbc33UMH3lhRX2UzOl\nQq60Ei4y2mRoUhftnIErfLPWQZp81TYH7UfGODDtz7sa89FStGc/iEZNiv7nB3Rb\nqBEdlPldspET5gVkY6TinrtMP9qsMdJ5iAPk1W/MUR6JpQUFbUNsFcYqvNadh2cG\nQjy7Va+c4ERbWeM/9BdLEl7aZemnKh4bFRn3p9zQnfeOEeSPlL+Pcoxo4kjcEtnv\nqU4Ts9WQOBfQflKUXlqMi8tULnD9EkwzbGJ6h/q3i5hnM0BGEz5rwFDfOgPkLcH+\nkR2hJ9Gc6bgMa3Qyf4hPZd03IfjAxDEIyFXy6tH/UeLZEfz7lQE6jCgE9s+voPaz\nANuy7PPL/z2XBPF3FWNJV2XPZ4GaFjtSb1D1OSDKsD5x2Z0zTE70ECofIHtxBFZh\nl1YwJe7m1ZV3Zo4cHrj+\n=SUgs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T10:11:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/platformatic/platformatic/commit/c39b1665eabde9442b65f4e4b52ad8f2e07fa56d","node_id":"C_kwDOIC2I7NoAKGMzOWIxNjY1ZWFiZGU5NDQyYjY1ZjRlNGI1MmFkOGYyZTA3ZmE1NmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/platformatic/platformatic/commit/e52551284c86e1fab1b3465ca90adf9add4072d6","sha":"e52551284c86e1fab1b3465ca90adf9add4072d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/e52551284c86e1fab1b3465ca90adf9add4072d6"}],"sha":"c39b1665eabde9442b65f4e4b52ad8f2e07fa56d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/c39b1665eabde9442b65f4e4b52ad8f2e07fa56d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71641154?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Simon-Lind-glitch/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Simon-Lind-glitch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Simon-Lind-glitch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Simon-Lind-glitch/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Simon-Lind-glitch","id":71641154,"login":"Simon-Lind-glitch","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNjQxMTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Simon-Lind-glitch/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Simon-Lind-glitch/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Simon-Lind-glitch/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Simon-Lind-glitch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Simon-Lind-glitch/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Simon-Lind-glitch","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/e52551284c86e1fab1b3465ca90adf9add4072d6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T07:40:34Z","email":"71641154+Simon-Lind-glitch@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Simon-Lind-glitch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T07:40:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(db-authorization): apply the find rule fields to where and orderBy (#5120)\n\nThe `fields` list of a find rule was only checked against the selected\nfields. The where clause and orderBy went straight to the mapper, so a\nrole that could not select a field could still filter or sort on it and\nrecover its value, e.g. with `where: { secret: { like: ''a%'' } }` or a few\n`gt`/`lt` calls. The same applied to count.\n\nfind and count now reject a user-supplied where (including `or` parts)\nor orderBy that references a field outside the rule''s `fields` with the\nexisting UnauthorizedField error. The check runs before the rule''s own\nchecks are merged in, so a rule can keep filtering on a field (e.g.\nuserId) that the user is not allowed to read.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-fable-5-1\n\nSigned-off-by: Simon Lind <s.lind.1991@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8a9d9bc08872d469d7f0f49506c10f8661477cde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/trees/8a9d9bc08872d469d7f0f49506c10f8661477cde"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/commits/e52551284c86e1fab1b3465ca90adf9add4072d6","verification":{"payload":"tree 8a9d9bc08872d469d7f0f49506c10f8661477cde\nparent 875a2662fc6484e066d9cfc677eb3c815a74a811\nauthor Simon-Lind-glitch <71641154+Simon-Lind-glitch@users.noreply.github.com> 1789458034 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789458034 -0700\n\nfix(db-authorization): apply the find rule fields to where and orderBy (#5120)\n\nThe `fields` list of a find rule was only checked against the selected\nfields. The where clause and orderBy went straight to the mapper, so a\nrole that could not select a field could still filter or sort on it and\nrecover its value, e.g. with `where: { secret: { like: ''a%'' } }` or a few\n`gt`/`lt` calls. The same applied to count.\n\nfind and count now reject a user-supplied where (including `or` parts)\nor orderBy that references a field outside the rule''s `fields` with the\nexisting UnauthorizedField error. The check runs before the rule''s own\nchecks are merged in, so a rule can keep filtering on a field (e.g.\nuserId) that the user is not allowed to read.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-fable-5-1\n\nSigned-off-by: Simon Lind <s.lind.1991@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqPZyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACssQALDbuI/FciCdUwNshGOJVCK7\ne6rwK9isgcB1dmUn6kqQBp5JkInEIvdBvkXxmkVCQkOgcB8dpkUoSBkQz1c3BtOz\ntEjuReVAOCI0RRVy1T5JKIrsaE8CqUQ0KfEr+8CyyIdhZxddnLNu15ssWu5qcTvC\naVaDJpqA5BdElh+NtjfFwX2XR2H1s48xfI16gMoO2+Wjhen99HtDHTU8C3gC7XpR\nPp9XOWfLfqk404DSaG11ZAP81rBVL93NO6lolRaXzCGkD47SpMSr7iSLxPDy1gr1\nWE5FtNhorrUssAxpyReP5Wf3LmX4+8MIj0ef9aMHPWmB6A3ZZJZwdZQPnQ8xYxxr\ntVJt1dQ65ZXnC9n5NVhzKBGTA5K2nuPjwrCFPP/qCOeNAgbdVMu3oHy6FxR/gzj0\np5IiTBQQiex5G+WfNz15QkzhbuH6fu2CEvOaUlRTefJyDg2xEWEebfDZzBV9UvGW\nPDfFQTjXbNV+SkuJWZuXWLZvMqEFkXie6RJORv+axUgsRcb6txrSvtvbW