s_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Simon-Lind-glitch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Simon-Lind-glitch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Simon-Lind-glitch/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Simon-Lind-glitch","id":71641154,"login":"Simon-Lind-glitch","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNjQxMTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Simon-Lind-glitch/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Simon-Lind-glitch/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Simon-Lind-glitch/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Simon-Lind-glitch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Simon-Lind-glitch/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Simon-Lind-glitch","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/875a2662fc6484e066d9cfc677eb3c815a74a811/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T13:45:52Z","email":"71641154+Simon-Lind-glitch@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Simon-Lind-glitch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T13:45:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(db-authorization): apply the find rule to count (#5118)\n\nsql-mapper entities expose a count method, used by the GraphQL count query\nand the REST X-Total-Count header, but db-authorization only hooked find,\nsave, insert, delete and updateMany. Any role could count every row\nregardless of its find rule, and a role with find: false could still count.\n\nThe new count hook resolves the user''s rule and applies the find rule''s\nwhere clause, honouring skipAuth and the no-ctx bypass like the other hooks.\nFields are not checked since a count returns no field data.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-fable-5-1\n\nSigned-off-by: Simon Lind <s.lind.1991@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"088c3f4bc153cbf560b3e17a755f792b227d7daa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/trees/088c3f4bc153cbf560b3e17a755f792b227d7daa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/commits/875a2662fc6484e066d9cfc677eb3c815a74a811","verification":{"payload":"tree 088c3f4bc153cbf560b3e17a755f792b227d7daa\nparent d1a685eff7bc6fc4bf7eecb1651c3b39ad2c7e4b\nauthor Simon-Lind-glitch <71641154+Simon-Lind-glitch@users.noreply.github.com> 1789393552 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789393552 -0700\n\nfix(db-authorization): apply the find rule to count (#5118)\n\nsql-mapper entities expose a count method, used by the GraphQL count query\nand the REST X-Total-Count header, but db-authorization only hooked find,\nsave, insert, delete and updateMany. Any role could count every row\nregardless of its find rule, and a role with find: false could still count.\n\nThe new count hook resolves the user''s rule and applies the find rule''s\nwhere clause, honouring skipAuth and the no-ctx bypass like the other hooks.\nFields are not checked since a count returns no field data.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-fable-5-1\n\nSigned-off-by: Simon Lind <s.lind.1991@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp/qQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKBoQAHY1Ikn/5LCOW8h7lAOSgsyK\nK8lKWBqgTwZErxlC/oKo6SB1cEuznBmx9jKs2Tm1R7IW9pDec+G63YLAEHDK6vlu\nbEMxamYNzDaKAm8BIwz1QnaQAFSXepC8dCTlbYWIUsINwcPnfEGxWNpCvy39G6gL\n3xyLBx6rkmUAC2GgAo9hE7xIWjUy0nNM6UIO2gXXc019NVw2iKeAk/53bnAhulbh\n8hNzMys6ey/m3+9v3UjTdKKVRZ0bLEk8mUD1Ruwy3+Z7el4+4K55Az3WzytYAE1X\nO/iOgl2WbhTry9jfEs9aOQ5bm4kF/0p4vlAMMOrUAq2ffMM7GtW4KEe9cyCfo+JN\n7DLuYKPeEGjDIy0Z4UlUnteSKzXmEIfDHiME5LiPllVMxL//tCcti/GCJ3Q7DFJr\nfasd9DRBSKp3oGSYqB8yIRZ1R1bDowrmttLG9TL1uQS704NbsAywHZZjSft56Gxx\nPrC7N6OidCPTynxsCLBtIc52oEdp/BdZ4MLNC+tn0OljdqtEEwkrdjKHVn9CSQhb\ndps1mn5N4vUq1MM+2Ccc7BsZTNYnldSRD2gBRKbz