cy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcollina","id":52195,"login":"mcollina","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/f1d5f176580766bd45c9ef550240892d7ac79e54/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T14:29:26Z","email":"hello@matteocollina.com","name":"Matteo Collina"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T14:29:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(wattpm-utils): compare canonical paths in the import checks (#5086)\n\nimportApplication decided whether the imported directory was already\nautoloaded and whether it lived inside the project with string prefix\ntests, so a sibling sharing a name prefix passed both.\n\nA sibling of the autoload directory, or anything nested deeper than one\nlevel below it, was reported as already autoloaded and the import\nsilently did nothing. A sibling of the project root was treated as being\ninside the repository, which recorded it as a ../ escaping relative path\nand dropped its Git URL, since entries inside the repository do not\ncarry one.\n\nCanonicalise the paths and replace the prefix tests: autoload only\nclaims the non excluded direct children of its directory, so match on\nthe parent rather than on containment at any depth, and use the\nrelative() boundary check for the repository. Compare canonical paths\nwhen looking up an already defined application too, so that a symlink\ndoes not produce a duplicate entry.\n\nFixes #5084\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5[1m]\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","tree":{"sha":"6ba39f4b793406a1dee21e70df3c20957bf74f63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/trees/6ba39f4b793406a1dee21e70df3c20957bf74f63"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/commits/f1d5f176580766bd45c9ef550240892d7ac79e54","verification":{"payload":"tree 6ba39f4b793406a1dee21e70df3c20957bf74f63\nparent 50e985973b2805cfbb1392c3ccf7fce830e28f62\nauthor Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com> 1788532166 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788532166 -0700\n\nfix(wattpm-utils): compare canonical paths in the import checks (#5086)\n\nimportApplication decided whether the imported directory was already\nautoloaded and whether it lived inside the project with string prefix\ntests, so a sibling sharing a name prefix passed both.\n\nA sibling of the autoload directory, or anything nested deeper than one\nlevel below it, was reported as already autoloaded and the import\nsilently did nothing. A sibling of the project root was treated as being\ninside the repository, which recorded it as a ../ escaping relative path\nand dropped its Git URL, since entries inside the repository do not\ncarry one.\n\nCanonicalise the paths and replace the prefix tests: autoload only\nclaims the non excluded direct children of its directory, so match on\nthe parent rather than on containment at any depth, and use the\nrelative() boundary check for the repository. Compare canonical paths\nwhen looking up an already defined application too, so that a symlink\ndoes not produce a duplicate entry.\n\nFixes #5084\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5[1m]\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","reason":"valid","s