l":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/platformatic/platformatic/commit/50e985973b2805cfbb1392c3ccf7fce830e28f62","node_id":"C_kwDOIC2I7NoAKDUwZTk4NTk3M2IyODA1Y2ZiYjEzOTJjM2NjZjdmY2U4MzBlMjhmNjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/platformatic/platformatic/commit/03f7999a25f4a86cd9baf84bbdee31af2cf690ef","sha":"03f7999a25f4a86cd9baf84bbdee31af2cf690ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/03f7999a25f4a86cd9baf84bbdee31af2cf690ef"}],"sha":"50e985973b2805cfbb1392c3ccf7fce830e28f62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/50e985973b2805cfbb1392c3ccf7fce830e28f62"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcollina","id":52195,"login":"mcollina","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/03f7999a25f4a86cd9baf84bbdee31af2cf690ef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:52:11Z","email":"hello@matteocollina.com","name":"Matteo Collina"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:52:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(runtime): resolve {PLT_<APPLICATION>_URL} against the applications that exist (#5096)\n\n`fetchApplicationUrl` was left without a consumer by #5083, because it could\nnot be applied to the configuration an application actually runs on: it\nmatched on the `_URL` suffix alone and always returned the URL of the\n*current* application, ignoring the variable name. Wiring it in turned the\n`valkey://{VALKEY_URL}` of packages/next/test/fixtures/caching-adapter into\n`valkey://http://frontend.plt.local`, and resolved a client pointing at\nanother application to the URL of the one doing the lookup.\n\nThe mapping is now built forwards, from the ids of the applications the\nruntime actually has to the variable each of them owns, using the same\nid-to-prefix convention generators already follow for `PLT_<PREFIX>_*`. A\nplaceholder resolves only when it names a real application, so\n`{PLT_WITH_LOGGER_URL}` yields `http://with-logger.plt.local` while\n`{VALKEY_URL}` and `{PLT_DATABASE_URL}` keep resolving to an empty string.\nBuilding it forwards also sidesteps the ambiguity of parsing the variable\nname, which is not reversible: `with-logger` and `with_logger` share a prefix.\n\nWith that guard in place the resolver is safe on the real load, so both\nconfiguration loads of a worker now resolve environment variables\nidentically, and applications can reference each other without the user\nsetting a variable per pair.\n\n`convertApplicationNameToPrefix` moves to @platformatic/foundation, so the\nruntime worker can share the convention without depending on the generators,\nand is re-exported from @platformatic/generators to keep its public API.\n\nFixes #5085\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","tree":{"sha":"295fd8e5c889d1974f931ef7343d192b97a2c2ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/trees/295fd8e5c889d1974f931ef7343d192b97a2c2ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/commits/03f7999a25f4a86cd9baf84bbdee31af2cf690ef","verification":{"payload":"tree 295fd8e5c889d1974f931ef7343d192b97a2c2ac\nparent c79942afc1b0582949a7ebc8f6da01098f2c2802\nauthor Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com> 1788529931 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788529931 -0700\n\nfix(runtime): resolve {PLT_<APPLICATION>_URL} against the applications that exist (#5096)\n\n`fetchApplicationUrl` was left without a consumer by #5083, because it could\nnot be applied to the configuration an application actually runs on: it\nmatched on the `_URL` suffix alone and always returned the URL of the\n*current* application, ignoring the variable name. Wiring it in turned the\n`valkey://{VALKEY_URL}` of packages/next/test/fixtures/caching-adapter into\n`valkey://http://frontend.plt.local`, and resolved a client pointing at\nanother application to the URL of the one doing the lookup.\n\nThe mapping is now built forwards, from the ids of the applications the\nruntime actually has to the variable each of them owns, using the same\nid-to-prefix convention generators already follow for `PLT_<PREFIX>_*`. A\nplaceholder resolves only when it names a real application, so\n`{PLT_WITH_LOGGER_URL}` yields `http://with-logger.plt.local` while\n`{VALKEY_URL}` and `{PLT_DATABASE_URL}` keep resolving to an empty string.\nBuilding it forwards also sidesteps the ambiguity of parsing the variable\nname, which is not reversible: `with-logger` and `with_logger` share a prefix.\n\nWith that guard in place the resolver is safe on the real load, so both\nconfiguration loads of a worker now resolve environment variables\nidentically, and applications can reference each other without the user\nsetting a variable per pair.\n\n`convertApplicationNameToPrefix` moves to @platformatic/foundation, so the\nruntime worker can share the convention without depending on the generators,\nand is re-exported from @platformatic/generators to keep its public API.\n\nFixes #5085\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqms0LCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcLMQAC64THZxoBuplRx055EPtSKE\n1ZEZ6BuMZeHHxpEP8ouPLKl0Ab+rla1wF8b7HdK1Akrf7XoEthDIhXKz2q/aLhIB\n3eLVyE3fqokdjt5UDpaA1pjA1n86Id/G0yBirB/heApSnCnGBEZvcbPRhkzzL/vd\n0uPcnkjTyXYETdpxySv5b138sq9/R7T5vVayagTpWG5G8nr5f3a1j/zpv8bhBEyb\noyum36to1+leMeClCmqR/tM5PDoPfu3VP4xRMf/0aWLkK8LR18VpQVJ66Z4TmtG4\nVpuF29K6PhUUc0gzLMQUY9+WU2ppDFTkYMedLL8b0LLrvQNxrHi3FhHXKYc88jhn\n70YIwuprShVb6PhouTIynrph0Qww4I11SKWyLgzxUCQQYo1XOUPx9QMVik8VZ2Wq\nTEGumzLvWIwwzRjUKzkTS5INhVPWtLorWeGC60Khd+kss98qCs657wf+NhRqSvkz\nDjnKHetnWmZ8SDjxpOxxomNZyqqQqkUsr5bFyF2mcu+TwqpvsbqZwnR+vBO5vHw5\nZMXm1k4mym/u55F73oPpxzU8HkRWV3IYx3ABRiw5JCQ1+qN5MWlq6nV17tR8ffMO\nmpCLTk2hfB8sR1u9+G5RqXVxgLifXN24nOp0Lm6KJtp3/BseM8i9YP6gbnY/CS0+\nJPfinpuMj/VxJgjuT4ab\n=yE9s\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-04T13:52:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false