/commits/fbdc7da11cbafa061bf3e23e83a1ad939b09ad60"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/604220?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leorossi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leorossi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leorossi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leorossi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/leorossi","id":604220,"login":"leorossi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNDIyMA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leorossi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leorossi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leorossi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leorossi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leorossi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leorossi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/9dda475b6d1e80adc4b09b890262f58596e4a51d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T19:01:38Z","email":"leonardo.rossi@gmail.com","name":"Leonardo Rossi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T19:01:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(gateway): let a gateway opt out of restarting on application changes (#5099)\n\n* feat(gateway): let a gateway opt out of restarting on application changes\n\nA gateway recomposes its routes by restarting itself whenever an application\nis added to or removed from the runtime. restartApplication replaces workers\none at a time, so with two or more workers and SO_REUSEPORT the listening\nsocket survives — but with ONE worker, which is the default and is forced\nwherever SO_REUSEPORT is unavailable, the runtime has no open port until the\nreplacement worker has booted.\n\nFor a gateway that does not route from the application registry at all — one\nthat resolves upstreams from shared state written by a runtime extension, for\ninstance — that restart recomposes nothing and costs the runtime its only\nport. Adding a version to such a runtime drops live traffic for the length of\na worker boot, twice when the change is a remove followed by an add.\n\ngateway.restartOnApplicationChange (default true) lets those gateways opt out.\nThe handler is not subscribed at all when it is false, rather than subscribed\nand then ignored, so nothing reaches the ITC either.\n\nThe default is unchanged, and a test pins it: every gateway that composes the\nregistry keeps exactly the behaviour it has today. The cost of opting out is\npinned too — a newly added application is not proxied until something else\nrestarts the gateway — because that is precisely what makes the option wrong\nfor a normal gateway.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Leonardo Rossi <leonardo.rossi@gmail.com>\n\n* test(gateway): record the new default in the resolved-config assertion\n\nget-config.test.js asserts the gateway''s resolved configuration exhaustively,\nso a new option with a schema default belongs in the expected object. Adding\nrestartOnApplicationChange there is the whole failure — the option itself is\ncovered by packages/runtime/test/gateway-restart-on-application-change.test.js.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Leonardo Rossi <leonardo.rossi@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Leonardo Rossi <leonardo.rossi@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b97ce456c474a4835c959d8590bb9cafb18bb774","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/trees/b97ce456c474a4835c959d8590bb9cafb18bb774"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/commits/9dda475b6d1e80adc4b09b890262f58596e4a51d","verification":{"payload":"tree b97ce456c474a4835c959d8590bb9cafb18bb774\nparent 4b80f25bf85b42133a5ab275fdd7666de9a04844\nauthor Leonardo Rossi <leonardo.rossi@gmail.com> 1787943698 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787943698 -0700\n\nfeat(gateway): let a gateway opt out of restarting on application changes (#5099)\n\n* feat(gateway): let a gateway opt out of restarting on application changes\n\nA gateway recomposes its routes by restarting itself whenever an application\nis added to or removed from the runtime. restartApplication replaces workers\none at a time, so with two or more workers and SO_REUSEPORT the listening\nsocket survives — but with ONE worker, which is the default and is forced\nwherever SO_REUSEPORT is unavailable, the runtime has no open port until the\nreplacement worker has booted.\n\nFor a gateway that does not route from the application registry at all — one\nthat resolves upstreams from shared state written by a runtime extension, for\ninstance — that restart recomposes nothing and costs the runtime its only\nport. Adding a version to such a runtime drops live traffic for the length of\na worker boot, twice when the change is a remove followed by an add.\n\ngateway.restartOnApplicationChange (default true) lets those gateways opt out.\nThe handler is not subscribed at all when it is false, rather than subscribed\nand then ignored, so nothing reaches the ITC either.\n\nThe default is unchanged, and a test pins it: every gateway that composes the\nregistry keeps exactly the behaviour it has today. The cost of opting out is\npinned too — a newly added application is not proxied until something else\nrestarts the gateway — because that is precisely what makes the option wrong\nfor a normal gateway.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Leonardo Rossi <leonardo.rossi@gmail.com>\n\n* test(gateway): record the new default in the resolved-config assertion\n\nget-config.test.js asserts the gateway''s resolved configuration exhaustively,\nso a new option with a schema default belongs in the expected object. Adding\nrestartOnApplicationChange there is the whole failure — the option itself is\ncovered by packages/runtime/test/gateway-restart-on-application-change.test.js.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nSigned-off-by: Leonardo Rossi <leonardo.rossi@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Leonardo Rossi <leonardo.rossi@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkdsSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARp0QAEHaw3/UQLae4U7OjAx60uPq\nI+1LGlfujtI4I0kvjySyU/wJWxIw1+/5N66Ar5XX3xQYLH9drwBKXOIcWBbqr2+0\nEwGW9cs4Jkf59fQBa4/LulBFJpQhfA5NU14l1PUoqevq1BTc9YifwSf2mta8enri\n5XlhoZVRXsv3eHcdtUiHRxO0gJ+vxkCejCO1X2AMiHa9U/kQQXYGdLTmn3Fztkwl\nUCUouAwIyUbQf21rm6sUqmFWJ9JyxPoIIqbQPNyDHkle+Kula2+qXXArqaCi/zlg\nFA0gmU1KZJ8hF2gVds9/2CCe7HaxwzPpO5Mr3EYk4NQYSuH9BjnxLGrcjZ9a9DKp\nCP1r5T4aWdfO8yM+/LE6vToORsIqogev0CaaGgR7Oq7PZRqUE752VATbEaczOKm7\nPVgRmDmlokmvCcUd2V9UAhDvfPQUVvGn21/BwV9W1/4+/4kiy9UfFAaKXqMTac/s\nfWEAmzBEE3BGG9ZD/UkXOdeHUyK1MpJc5w4twz3q4oOvoGY0rTLaI7ewg7LYOaLl\npViUy/V7k81ruuvdVJIMm05gY4oPcAf7FTI1bc2MgOyBs7kHUfCSjFE2ItsgdstX\nCQP438goEvX1Id99Rnwy+8nsNSyuTjYYWFYoEH2Y7uxf1qfXjhF6Vau815HPjI/a\n8X/b2PuZN7tdSB+EvH38\n=/8ff\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T19:01:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web