events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikaelkaron/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikaelkaron/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikaelkaron/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikaelkaron/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mikaelkaron","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/e2a905e9c671093fa80b605d18c98873d32ce0bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T13:32:10Z","email":"mikael@karon.se","name":"Mikael Karon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T13:32:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gateway): keep body-less response status codes in the composed OpenAPI document (#5053)\n\nA response which declares no `content` - a 204, a 304, or any other status code\nwhose response object has no body - is dropped by\n@platformatic/fastify-openapi-glue while it registers the composed routes. The\ndocument @fastify/swagger regenerates from those routes then reports `200:\nDefault Response` for an operation whose responses were all body-less, and\nsilently loses the status code for one which also has a response with a body.\n\nThe glue keeps those status codes when `addEmptySchema` is enabled, and as of\n5.2.0 it registers them with a `{ type: ''null'' }` schema, which @fastify/swagger\nturns back into a response object without `content`. Enable it unconditionally:\nthe response schemas only shape the document, since every composed route answers\nwith the stream @fastify/reply-from proxies and Fastify does not serialize\nstreams.\n\nThe `addEmptySchema` gateway option is therefore redundant and is now documented\nas deprecated.\n\nSigned-off-by: Mikael Karon <mikael@karon.se>\nSigned-off-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"37e26fd3f33a5aa3188d8e486ff6ecf7a9ef7e86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/trees/37e26fd3f33a5aa3188d8e486ff6ecf7a9ef7e86"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/commits/e2a905e9c671093fa80b605d18c98873d32ce0bb","verification":{"payload":"tree 37e26fd3f33a5aa3188d8e486ff6ecf7a9ef7e86\nparent 8a45b42453bf08eadbafa6abb4e95894b1cde804\nauthor Mikael Karon <mikael@karon.se> 1786109530 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786109530 -0700\n\nfix(gateway): keep body-less response status codes in the composed OpenAPI document (#5053)\n\nA response which declares no `content` - a 204, a 304, or any other status code\nwhose response object has no body - is dropped by\n@platformatic/fastify-openapi-glue while it registers the composed routes. The\ndocument @fastify/swagger regenerates from those routes then reports `200:\nDefault Response` for an operation whose responses were all body-less, and\nsilently loses the status code for one which also has a response with a body.\n\nThe glue keeps those status codes when `addEmptySchema` is enabled, and as of\n5.2.0 it registers them with a `{ type: ''null'' }` schema, which @fastify/swagger\nturns back into a response object without `content`. Enable it unconditionally:\nthe response schemas only shape the document, since every composed route answers\nwith the stream @fastify/reply-from proxies and Fastify does not serialize\nstreams.\n\nThe `addEmptySchema` gateway option is therefore redundant and is now documented\nas deprecated.\n\nSigned-off-by: Mikael Karon <mikael@karon.se>\nSigned-off-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdd5aCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAY4gQABi3917k3ZQeRwhgslgdGYcM\nHsgo9ZqD8+ZbZjugR8qEwbgaYrSA1ZySNBErgoaipPNyRqNSNBugXQaaTymDS7yc\nmy2lQ69LX1KmPLCgJk+SPdt2All1y6s2clR4lAi65kGtbReQnVBh/tJoAuR+FwRl\n6q9iIy1VbejaOXOOn39gBtWmzPYQfoFj3cnZLSbgpK3+ubk1OVv2OB0Ntgz6i0jW\nFrvDCoKgSM7Bquc8JaLHpOUUXrwUowMzRZsRlW99KUQv8GXdTSchJcDu5SyCrSj+\nfI2h/WQhcod9Gc7mRx0EX1GlhImET6L0192wTJqT+