allabet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akallabet/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Akallabet","id":2728023,"login":"Akallabet","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MjgwMjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akallabet/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akallabet/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akallabet/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akallabet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akallabet/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Akallabet","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/e1f69f164752ba4c15cccd73984bb5d93fec675d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T09:43:41Z","email":"grazianos86@gmail.com","name":"Graziano Statello"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T09:43:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(sql-openapi): support contains, contained and overlaps for array fields (#5060)\n\n* feat(sql-openapi): support overlaps where clause for array fields\n\nArray fields only exposed the ''all'' and ''any'' modifiers in the generated\nquerystring schema, so ''where.<field>.overlaps'' was silently stripped by\nthe schema validation (removeAdditional) and the filter was never applied,\neven though sql-mapper already supports the ''&&'' operator.\n\nExpose the ''overlaps'' modifier for array fields and split its\ncomma-separated value into an array in both the list (GET) and\nupdateMany (PUT) handlers, mirroring the in/nin handling.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-fable-5\nSigned-off-by: Akallabet <grazianos86@gmail.com>\n\n* feat(sql-openapi): support contains and contained for array fields\n\nExtend the array-field where support to the remaining array-to-array\ncomparators sql-mapper already implements: contains (@>) and\ncontained (<@). Like overlaps, they take a comma-separated list of\nvalues, so they are declared as strings in the querystring schema and\nsplit in the list and updateMany handlers.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-fable-5\nSigned-off-by: Akallabet <grazianos86@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Akallabet <grazianos86@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"ac1be78809c989e28a6f86903d1ee375be1a8973","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/trees/ac1be78809c989e28a6f86903d1ee375be1a8973"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/commits/e1f69f164752ba4c15cccd73984bb5d93fec675d","verification":{"payload":"tree ac1be78809c989e28a6f86903d1ee375be1a8973\nparent eb0b29c1956f6da41e69a96275857682efd90389\nauthor Graziano Statello <grazianos86@gmail.com> 1785923021 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785923021 -0700\n\nfeat(sql-openapi): support contains, contained and overlaps for array fields (#5060)\n\n* feat(sql-openapi): support overlaps where clause for array fields\n\nArray fields only exposed the ''all'' and ''any'' modifiers in the generated\nquerystring schema, so ''where.<field>.overlaps'' was silently stripped by\nthe schema validation (removeAdditional) and the filter was never applied,\neven though sql-mapper already supports the ''&&'' operator.\n\nExpose the ''overlaps'' modifier for array fields and split its\ncomma-separated value into an array in both the list (GET) and\nupdateMany (PUT) handlers, mirroring the in/nin handling.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-fable-5\nSigned-off-by: Akallabet <grazianos86@gmail.com>\n\n* feat(sql-openapi): support contains and contained for array fields\n\nExtend the array-field where support to the remaining array-to-array\ncomparators sql-mapper already implements: contains (@>) and\ncontained (<@). Like overlaps, they take a comma-separated list of\nvalues, so they are declared as strings in the querystring schema and\nsplit in the list and updateMany handlers.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-fable-5\nSigned-off-by: Akallabet <grazianos86@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Akallabet <grazianos86@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcwXNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKTIQAFRrvtRNj39AxV3UWvEwuE0s\nVyynegJ8qnMUVjWcmF6MjfW7J1kb/xsMfYFzQ7QCcf5O1Vq3kFFbXYkW7VhdKuX6\npi7Vf2i9+S6P2reh3LcnozqioLxYiOatbGMgpWhIlUjtBWL92uAd3axZMrvXJxaB\nJsxYYvZL99YV+pASiND6zHNaYKzoEnPt1jiFt3gYCBk7Wl9YUTR49a+ZDL48ALkL\npUfExQlks714qYpx0ENTy/hpmBTKJM4HD1OkaA+3CMh9c9m6wrhtvb2QJtmOJPjP\nPx02j/ihp2oFFDBspKK5/d98+6Y7PtMKPSyLDQu6Djw5madcJknQo/VmRkfQ94A7\noSh73Rt3EoYjuxFFk7jAg1JCeW7bKsKCb4OVIGxoumlufcJC/FPrYQ7pQ/Lmlafh\nX720UXJI5kktX+T3wt18jwzyHBlDfFphrbPNRrfDDp6tpM2WHV5DviCMV0nrrhjT\n0ElbPVAQFKnJdvVn1U1qmzsezSN4i+LAyyFtpXOTXhourzQ2uKp5JrUl0zp0sseb\n57uRx2EFcMD8q4UMaueMJQYUeba6dopXKq4gGeglPsGszmwp0EqLY4nnAsQys+Wn\nFCgB6ncsZDdsbChPvYVjlLn4Bw1cKR0hifm3CPbk3Z0ULRK6TvD3dRei2QroAsyt\nEMPzfngC2UuA+V3sPSTJ\n=fy9s\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-05T09:43:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"htm