"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/platformatic/platformatic/commit/176fafe6c941575f1ff06f94c3b988b8a104a4b6","node_id":"C_kwDOIC2I7NoAKDE3NmZhZmU2Yzk0MTU3NWYxZmYwNmY5NGMzYjk4OGI4YTEwNGE0YjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/platformatic/platformatic/commit/50cffb8b3e37313b132a51c80b4017f91b198658","sha":"50cffb8b3e37313b132a51c80b4017f91b198658","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/50cffb8b3e37313b132a51c80b4017f91b198658"}],"sha":"176fafe6c941575f1ff06f94c3b988b8a104a4b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/176fafe6c941575f1ff06f94c3b988b8a104a4b6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcollina","id":52195,"login":"mcollina","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/50cffb8b3e37313b132a51c80b4017f91b198658/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T10:33:02Z","email":"hello@matteocollina.com","name":"Matteo Collina"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T10:33:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: check the licenses of production dependencies (#5046)\n\nAdds a license check to CI, modelled on the one Fastify runs through\nfastify/workflows nested-quality.yml, and a generated list of the licenses of\nevery production dependency we ship.\n\nFastify''s check is a single license-checker invocation with an --onlyAllow\nlist. That does not work here: the root package.json is private and only has\ndevDependencies, so license-checker --production at the root finds nothing.\nThe real production graph hangs off the 39 workspace packages. scripts/\nlicense-check.js walks that graph instead, resolving each dependency the way\nNode does, which works both with the hoisted layout this repo configures and\nwith pnpm''s symlinked one. It has no dependencies of its own.\n\nThe allow list is Fastify''s seven licenses (0BSD, Apache-2.0, BlueOak-1.0.0,\nBSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, MIT) plus Python-2.0, which argparse needs.\nNothing else is pre-approved, so a dependency that introduces a new license\nfails CI until the license is reviewed and added explicitly. SPDX expressions\nare evaluated properly, including OR, AND, parentheses, WITH and the fact\nthat AND binds tighter than OR.\n\nOnly dependencies and optionalDependencies are traversed. devDependencies are\nnot shipped, and peerDependencies (next, astro, vite and friends) are\ninstalled by the user rather than by us.\n\nTwo licenses fall outside the base list and are now documented with the\npackages responsible for them:\n\n- LGPL-3.0-or-later, from the prebuilt libvips binaries (@img/sharp-libvips-*)\n  that sharp pulls in as platform specific optional dependencies. The only\n  Platformatic package affected is @platformatic/next, through\n  @platformatic/image-optimizer. The exception is scoped to that route: it\n  names the exact license expression, and the checker verifies the constraint\n  structurally by removing @platformatic/image-optimizer from the graph and\n  re-walking from every workspace package. If an LGPL dependency ever becomes\n  reachable another way, the exception stops applying and CI fails.\n\n- Python-2.0, from argparse via js-yaml, reaching @platformatic/composer,\n  @platformatic/db, @platformatic/db-core, @platformatic/gateway and\n  @platformatic/sql-mapper.\n\nThree more dependencies (rc, type-fest, expand-template) carry OR expressions\nthat the base list satisfies through MIT.\n\nTHIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md lists all 569 production dependencies with their\nlicense and repository, a summary by license, and a section attributing every\nlicense outside the base list to the packages that depend on it. CI regenerates\nit and uploads it as an artifact, so the list is available even when the check\nfails. It is not diffed against the committed copy, because prebuilt binaries\nare platform specific and the file would otherwise churn on every platform and\nevery dependency bump.\n\nVerified: the SPDX evaluator passes 25 cases including GPL-3.0,\nLGPL-3.0-or-later, (MIT AND GPL-3.0), unparenthesised precedence and\nSEE LICENSE IN LICENSE; a fixture package depending on an LGPL binary directly\nis rejected with the reason the exception does not apply; a fixture\nintroducing CC0-1.0 is rejected; the Linux variants of the sharp binaries were\nchecked against the registry, so the ubuntu-24.04 job agrees with the local\nrun.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","tree":{"sha":"7536fd76d8ea4cca06d39968e8541df3a64d7418","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/trees/7536fd76d8ea4cca06d39968e8541df3a64d7418"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/commits/50cffb8b3e37313b132a51c80b4017f91b198658","verification":{"payload":"tree 7536fd76d8ea4cca06d39968e8541df3a64d7418\nparent a76af7751a82cee151ee81ab5906f13379f92f3e\nauthor Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com> 1785493982 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785493982 -0700\n\nci: check the licenses of production dependencies (#5046)\n\nAdds a license check to CI, modelled on the one Fastify runs through\nfastify/workflows nested-quality.yml, and a generated list of the licenses of\nevery production dependency we ship.\n\nFastify''s check is a single license-checker invocation with an --onlyAllow\nlist. That does not work here: the root package.json is private and only has\ndevDependencies, so license-checker --production at the root finds nothing.\nThe real production graph hangs off the 39 workspace packages. scripts/\nlicense-check.js walks that graph instead, resolving each dependency the way\nNode does, which works both with the hoisted layout this repo configures and\nwith pnpm''s symlinked one. It has no dependencies of its own.\n\nThe allow list is Fastify''s seven licenses (0BSD, Apache-2.0, BlueOak-1.0.0,\nBSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, MIT) plus Python-2.0, which argparse needs.\nNothing else is pre-approved, so a dependency that introduces a new license\nfails CI until the license is reviewed and added explicitly. SPDX expressions\nare evaluated properly, including OR, AND, parentheses, WITH and the fact\nthat AND binds tighter than OR.\n\nOnly dependencies and optionalDependencies are traversed. devDependencies are\nnot shipped, and peerDependencies (next, astro, vite and friends) are\ninstalled by the user rather than by us.\n\nTwo licenses fall outside the base list and are now documented with the\npackages responsible for them:\n\n- LGPL-3.0-or-later, from the prebuilt libvips binaries (@img/sharp-libvips-*)\n  that sharp pulls in as platform specific optional dependencies. The only\n  Platformatic package affected is @platformatic/next, through\n  @platformatic/image-optimizer. The exception is scoped to that route: it\n  names the exact license expression, and the checker verifies the constraint\n  structurally by removing @platformatic/image-optimizer from the graph and\n  re-walking from every workspace package. If an LGPL dependency ever becomes\n  reachable another way, the exception stops applying and CI fails.\n\n- Python-2.0, from argparse via js-yaml, reaching @platformatic/composer,\n  @platformatic/db, @platformatic/db-core, @platformatic/gateway and\n  @platformatic/sql-mapper.\n\nThree more dependencies (rc, type-fest, expand-template) carry OR expressions\nthat the base list satisfies through MIT.\n\nTHIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md lists all 569 production dependencies with their\nlicense and repository, a summary by license, and a section attributing every\nlicense outside the base list to the packages that depend on it. CI regenerates\nit and uploads it as an artifact, so the list is available even when the check\nfails. It is not diffed against the committed copy, because prebuilt binaries\nare platform specific and the file would otherwise churn on every platform and\nevery dependency bump.\n\nVerified: the SPDX evaluator passes 25 cases including GPL-3.0,\nLGPL-3.0-or-later, (MIT AND GPL-3.0), unparenthesised precedence and\nSEE LICENSE IN LICENSE; a fixture package depending on an LGPL binary directly\nis rejected with the reason the exception does not apply; a fixture\nintroducing CC0-1.0 is rejected; the Linux variants of the sharp binaries were\nchecked against the registry, so the ubuntu-24.04 job agrees with the local\nrun.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbHneCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxMQQAJBTfITrc2gn+ITgiPywJHr5\nBY2/