ype":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/platformatic/platformatic/commit/b102f6639a166ba0bef2b5dff0914b9cd95de2c8","node_id":"C_kwDOIC2I7NoAKGIxMDJmNjYzOWExNjZiYTBiZWYyYjVkZmYwOTE0YjljZDk1ZGUyYzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/platformatic/platformatic/commit/e68bfe0e49bde7792d2039787e1926f27d7fc35e","sha":"e68bfe0e49bde7792d2039787e1926f27d7fc35e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/e68bfe0e49bde7792d2039787e1926f27d7fc35e"}],"sha":"b102f6639a166ba0bef2b5dff0914b9cd95de2c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/b102f6639a166ba0bef2b5dff0914b9cd95de2c8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcollina","id":52195,"login":"mcollina","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/e68bfe0e49bde7792d2039787e1926f27d7fc35e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T14:39:40Z","email":"hello@matteocollina.com","name":"Matteo Collina"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-29T14:39:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: complete Phase 6 — Explanation quadrant and verified migration guides (#5041)\n\nAdds the missing Diátaxis Explanation quadrant and the migration guides the\nrestructure plan has called for since the start.\n\nNew `docs/concepts/`, wired into the sidebar as its own top-level category:\n\n- watt-architecture.md   why the platform is shaped this way, and what it\n                         trades away\n- multithread-model.md   threads vs processes, what isolation you actually\n                         get, and the process-boundary failure mode\n- application-lifecycle.md  dependency-level startup, entrypoint-first\n                         shutdown, crash restart vs unhealthy replacement\n- modular-monolith.md    what the term means and when to stop using one\n\nNew `docs/learn/migrations/` with staged Express and Fastify guides. Both were\nexecuted rather than written from the seed doc: a real Express 5 app wrapped\nwith zero code changes, a two-application project exchanging data over\n`*.plt.local`, and a Fastify application behind a gateway.\n\nThat last one surfaced behaviour documented nowhere outside the test fixtures:\nthe gateway strips its prefix before the request reaches the application, so a\nmigrated app keeps its original routes — and adding the prefix produces a 404\nthat reads like a routing bug. `node.absoluteUrl: true` inverts this. Mixing\nthe two modes fails in both directions.\n\nEvery claim in the concepts pages was read out of source rather than\nparaphrased from existing docs: topological start levels from runtime.js and\nutils.js, health defaults from foundation/lib/schema.js, the restart bounds\nfrom the MAX_BOOTSTRAP_ATTEMPTS constants, and the `.plt.local` MessagePort\nhop from worker/interceptors.js.\n\nCloses the TypeScript guide split as \"will not do\" — `plt service compile` and\n`plt runtime compile` no longer exist, so the single file is the right shape.\nSkips the example gallery, whose stated precondition (CI-tested examples) has\nnothing to point at.\n\nAlso fixes seven broken links a stricter sweep found, including two resolving\nto bare directories with no page behind them, and a quoted log transcript in\nbuild-modular-monolith.md still showing the pre-Phase-4 URL that\npackages/db no longer emits.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5[1m]\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","tree":{"sha":"75711849234520154d4819adfe18b5a928acdcc0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/trees/75711849234520154d4819adfe18b5a928acdcc0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/commits/e68bfe0e49bde7792d2039787e1926f27d7fc35e","verification":{"payload":"tree 75711849234520154d4819adfe18b5a928acdcc0\nparent 07d598e1decfff078a2a1d40741cb9a8337b814c\nauthor Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com> 1785335980 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785335980 -0700\n\ndocs: complete Phase 6 — Explanation quadrant and verified migration guides (#5041)\n\nAdds the missing Diátaxis Explanation quadrant and the migration guides the\nrestructure plan has called for since the start.\n\nNew `docs/concepts/`, wired into the sidebar as its own top-level category:\n\n- watt-architecture.md   why the platform is shaped this way, and what it\n                         trades away\n- multithread-model.md   threads vs processes, what isolation you actually\n                         get, and the process-boundary failure mode\n- application-lifecycle.md  dependency-level startup, entrypoint-first\n                         shutdown, crash restart vs unhealthy replacement\n- modular-monolith.md    what the term means and when to stop using one\n\nNew `docs/learn/migrations/` with staged Express and Fastify guides. Both were\nexecuted rather than written from the seed doc: a real Express 5 app wrapped\nwith zero code changes, a two-application project exchanging data over\n`*.plt.local`, and a Fastify application behind a gateway.\n\nThat last one surfaced behaviour documented nowhere outside the test fixtures:\nthe gateway strips its prefix before the request reaches the application, so a\nmigrated app keeps its original routes — and adding the prefix produces a 404\nthat reads like a routing bug. `node.absoluteUrl: true` inverts this. Mixing\nthe two modes fails in both directions.\n\nEvery claim in the concepts pages was read out of source rather than\nparaphrased from existing docs: topological start levels from runtime.js and\nutils.js, health defaults from foundation/lib/schema.js, the restart bounds\nfrom the MAX_BOOTSTRAP_ATTEMPTS constants, and the `.plt.local` MessagePort\nhop from worker/interceptors.js.\n\nCloses the TypeScript guide split as \"will not do\" — `plt service compile` and\n`plt runtime compile` no longer exist, so the single file is the right shape.\nSkips the example gallery, whose stated precondition (CI-tested examples) has\nnothing to point at.\n\nAlso fixes seven broken links a stricter sweep found, including two resolving\nto bare directories with no page behind them, and a quoted log transcript in\nbuild-modular-monolith.md still showing the pre-Phase-4 URL that\npackages/db no longer emits.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5[1m]\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqahCsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2boQACRFe6Se0hI69O+8Yth/2FcX\nwLyOqzUOim20JrBr7rSCrUIqMGIrJ7AnH1Jt7lmJWW6uoU15ojXI08k/HSaZNXkt\npguJP4XepC0W1Zh60kz3xDHfZkmeeCERO9QtxZXrhkrxpXjuxffUROAAzJl7j0mj\nxukGur8MS4g1R2J1urzGGX2s4yJnsNN83uQzItEpduAF2/v2xhxUJVlEE9fCxeaK\nBGbF+QUtMD7Ml7gqZP+w1qXHIqK7Cs3/Ax0zq7Th3ReTFWCbaBvkScZPrTZy2ZAQ\nb1g609NVCwJUzLLjg6BJZtfjH27cWNa8wEZj4lHpbGd+PC/4f6wD8hwtOsrY1XRD\nhXPgQcbzuR9wHf/LdrrsGrqNsnhGITRZX9OJb4CGn48mPa5Y005IYl4Asfprbrfq\nrhVJnvuj6SaOZsVVWE9KyJ7WCIZjXr+i8AGhnuRQjs4+O8M97YFjvqGYADBeI/Ba\nYvEpuhQIDpwWGDf1JYI/U0iu7JiN7NOdA0cJB/yaxHNSroXcCJ37ZbR3ivAKe/lk\nVRIpVSysTV+5jsox75pkm8i7XXEZbbTmmkbCtQxPcAt0gkLx9AxxeFh4F29cbV4w\nD8YkXT4tD+6N5+VtfPRR7R946Ww+XBz/WgzxNl5zxRlXDgn3A9pE00vk6S3sWLmJ\n1Roh43sfn4UqyAyAsAm3\n=kh2t\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-29T14:39:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/platformatic/platformatic/commit/e68bfe0e49bde7792d2039787e1926f27d7fc35e","node_id":"C_kwDOIC2I7NoAKGU2OGJmZTBlNDliZGU3NzkyZDIwMzk3ODdlMTkyNmYyN2Q3ZmMzNWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/platformatic/platformatic/commit/07d598e1decfff078a2a1d40741cb9a8337b814c","sha":"07d598e1decfff078a2a1d40741cb9a8337b814c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/07d598e1decfff078a2a1d40741cb9a8337b814c"}],"sha":"e68bfe0e49bde7792d2039787e1926f27d7fc35e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/e68bfe0e49bde7792d2039787e1926f27d7fc35e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcollina","id":52195,"login":"mcollina","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/07d598e1decfff078a2a1d40741cb9a8337b814c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T14:38:52Z","email":"hello@matteocollina.com","name":"Matteo Collina"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-29T14:38:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: fix five defects in the CRUD tutorial, verified against PostgreSQL (#5043)\n\nThe Todo API tutorial had never been executed. Running it end to end — against\nPostgreSQL 15 in Docker and against the default SQLite path — turned up five\ndefects. The SQLite main line worked; everything offered as an alternative did\nnot.\n\n**Step numbering.** Steps ran 2, 4, 5, 6, 7. There was no Step 1 and no Step 3.\nRenumbered 1-5.\n\n**The PostgreSQL connection string was never read.** The tutorial said to set\n`DATABASE_URL`. The variable is `PLT_DB_DATABASE_URL` — named after the\napplication id, and referenced as `{PLT_DB_DATABASE_URL}` in web/db/watt.json.\nSetting `DATABASE_URL` raises no error and has no effect: migrations silently\nkeep going to db.sqlite while Postgres stays empty. Fixed, with a caution\nexplaining the naming and how to tell which database you are really using.\n\n**The migration SQL could not run on PostgreSQL.** The tutorial invites you to\nswitch to Postgres and then hands you SQLite-only DDL:\n\n  - `DATETIME`            -> type \"datetime\" does not exist\n  - `BOOLEAN DEFAULT 0`   -> default expression is of type integer\n  - `INTEGER PRIMARY KEY` -> creates fine, but is not auto-increment, so the\n                             tutorial''s own \"Test Your API\" step fails with a\n                             not-null violation\n\nBoth migrations now carry SQLite/PostgreSQL tabs, plus a table explaining the\nthree differences and noting that the auto-increment one is the dangerous one\nbecause it fails at first POST rather than at migration time.\n\n**The CORS step crashed the runtime.** It instructed adding `cors` to\n`server` in the root watt.json. The runtime schema rejects it:\n\n    - /server: must NOT have additional properties\n\nCORS is answered by the application serving the request, so it belongs in\nweb/db/watt.json. Fixed, with the failure quoted and a curl command to confirm\nthe header.\n\n**Wrong filename.** The architecture table cited web/db/platformatic.json; the\nwizard writes web/db/watt.json.\n\nVerified after fixing: clean database, migrations applied, POST /todos returns\n200 with id 1, a second POST returns id 2 (proving SERIAL auto-increment where\nINTEGER PRIMARY KEY would have failed), CORS returns\naccess-control-allow-origin, and /users, /documentation and /graphql all 200.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5[1m]\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","tree":{"sha":"2f122401a5cb1f5ce7fb1eaf61489105ed34f1fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/trees/2f122401a5cb1f5ce7fb1eaf61489105ed34f1fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/commits/07d598e1decfff078a2a1d40741cb9a8337b814c","verification":{"payload":"tree 2f122401a5cb1f5ce7fb1eaf61489105ed34f1fe\nparent 57e5c19fd7b00d4c5c1a30aa70679b0d1fdb4671\nauthor Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com> 1785335932 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785335932 -0700\n\ndocs: fix five defects in the CRUD tutorial, verified against PostgreSQL (#5043)\n\nThe Todo API tutorial had never been executed. Running it end to end — against\nPostgreSQL 15 in Docker and against the default SQLite path — turned up five\ndefects. The SQLite main line worked; everything offered as an alternative did\nnot.\n\n**Step numbering.** Steps ran 2, 4, 5, 6, 7. There was no Step 1 and no Step 3.\nRenumbered 1-5.\n\n**The PostgreSQL connection string was never read.** The tutorial said to set\n`DATABASE_URL`. The variable is `PLT_DB_DATABASE_URL` — named after the\napplication id, and referenced as `{PLT_DB_DATABASE_URL}` in web/db/watt.json.\nSetting `DATABASE_URL` raises no error and has no effect: migrations silently\nkeep going to db.sqlite while Postgres stays empty. Fixed, with a caution\nexplaining the naming and how to tell which database you are really using.\n\n**The migration SQL could not run on PostgreSQL.** The tutorial invites you to\nswitch to Postgres and then hands you SQLite-only DDL:\n\n  - `DATETIME`            -> type \"datetime\" does not exist\n  - `BOOLEAN DEFAULT 0`   -> default expression is of type integer\n  - `INTEGER PRIMARY KEY` -> creates fine, but is not auto-increment, so the\n                             tutorial''s own \"Test Your API\" step fails with a\n                             not-null violation\n\nBoth migrations now carry SQLite/PostgreSQL tabs, plus a table explaining the\nthree differences and noting that the auto-increment one is the dangerous one\nbecause it fails at first POST rather than at migration time.\n\n**The CORS step crashed the runtime.** It instructed adding `cors` to\n`server` in the root watt.json. The runtime schema rejects it:\n\n    - /server: must NOT have additional properties\n\nCORS is answered by the application serving the request, so it belongs in\nweb/db/watt.json. Fixed, with the failure quoted and a curl command to confirm\nthe header.\n\n**Wrong filename.** The architecture table cited web/db/platformatic.json; the\nwizard writes web/db/watt.json.\n\nVerified after fixing: clean database, migrations applied, POST /todos returns\n200 with id 1, a second POST returns id 2 (proving SERIAL auto-increment where\nINTEGER PRIMARY KEY would have failed), CORS returns\naccess-control-allow-origin, and /users, /documentation and /graphql all 200.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5[1m]\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqahB8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA29sQAEjuPDB71T6YjnaWmZ5rAnCd\nHQ0ctsMQ5rKMw72MKrU3zLiwtYla6imhcod6jSDMOJfRyGxY0dthHOjs8VQB67xL\npulN8LICXN3YCyhuJmSsrK3ZJNG4wj8oDST/iMt//C7jZqgubwqPi6DnvqlO/iz3\nvnbb28LTrjstU35HoJOxW4CbWNUcAkWybwOZtuhOAVjJngdAf1ANJMsTxhduuQ45\nexjucbOHY4rxaRO/XHDtffXdzK7KUoCswZ3rEnOdJ5eGisb/zcs2o+rN8+JbNjIL\nAGppUFEZa3kcvKBQBYz6kTpRxob5EKxkvfujUuOLz7Qkzr5GEPqzCux8v+kRYJN9\nuVc7QdHj2H8DfDiwnpQEK8AC4uRfabP46aqS43vqfgsgt0zwdg60VbTsSkTAhNth\nGW5znpw+dV/3ejOB0Bg2bWI/DmQpHzOoNt4KMA159BV2S4ffi8Dy85w41CKwkWzm\n7Ags9usjkyHu1LmDSsSvPYPOFCOhzZxtpmWvy4PlGTjK4p9oGaXnY0qKgVxTXOm7\n1ez4lMHPDLgI1YOlNQ1uJDaoh5aECULr/qOZD4uuDkmqsvRJx1QZO6VF/qGYrHn0\ntMSWtyKFP4PUqwGJTSuFBXgoSxgKEzY4m+g+ICeUACRsg3BQQXSJ3/bQAByRx1Cg\nk3+AlUuUK2gB3wgK8KEb\n=htjO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-29T14:38:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/platformatic/platformatic/commit/07d598e1decfff078a2a1d40741cb9a8337b814c","node_id":"C_kwDOIC2I7NoAKDA3ZDU5OGUxZGVjZmZmMDc4YTJhMWQ0MDc0MWNiOWE4MzM3YjgxNGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/platformatic/platformatic/commit/57e5c19fd7b00d4c5c1a30aa70679b0d1fdb4671","sha":"57e5c19fd7b00d4c5c1a30aa70679b0d1fdb4671","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/57e5c19fd7b00d4c5c1a30aa70679b0d1fdb4671"}],"sha":"07d598e1decfff078a2a1d40741cb9a8337b814c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/07d598e1decfff078a2a1d40741cb9a8337b814c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcollina","id":52195,"login":"mcollina","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/57e5c19fd7b00d4c5c1a30aa70679b0d1fdb4671/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T14:38:42Z","email":"hello@matteocollina.com","name":"Matteo Collina"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-29T14:38:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add lint:fix script to all packages and root workspace (#5038)\n\nAdd ''lint:fix'' script (eslint --fix) in every package that has a lint\nscript, plus a root workspace script to run it across all packages.\n\nAssisted-by: Pi\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","tree":{"sha":"b23e8eaea1187116c28db3cf0b8b2120984078df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/trees/b23e8eaea1187116c28db3cf0b8b2120984078df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/commits/57e5c19fd7b00d4c5c1a30aa70679b0d1fdb4671","verification":{"payload":"tree b23e8eaea1187116c28db3cf0b8b2120984078df\nparent 62fe5733b3e798d166aa42eb0525fa910dbf3022\nauthor Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com> 1785335922 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785335922 -0700\n\nfeat: add lint:fix script to all packages and root workspace (#5038)\n\nAdd ''lint:fix'' script (eslint --fix) in every package that has a lint\nscript, plus a root workspace script to run it across all packages.\n\nAssisted-by: Pi\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqahByCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABgwQAEnDIxXlldGBJgW8wb4FG2ba\n4WU+OR6Jqb5ja9vHS5IWMNyeqsF+sgJwlJBa1o3FAvYuKyZagvs0XKJgqAN4lrpd\nBMx2XO+wfPmkJBtXD1OxMmmFPYgKaDOpu+okrlHduBkgy9QlyPwyvKtfgehx3muA\ne6rshmwW8cd5aFHokYscxi3bwcOc/3iNbs6hZfWuE+mb2/r6q9Nr7Mew7bM19wJ1\noT+rt+mPNeGnzvdRFAL976Bsw35AEo/CI1i51cweDasD4MxiKdtTvJgALoJG+ML0\n12A1qy2tbWfEWEAFQzgyVVOsbfBwysoehuGMn+wOPiZdebRrY8FD0o1hwhHwrhZ4\naCfqEqT/LXzW2Wr62CMrD44trcJI3DzT9AR+qZ3alpJEuAPDmXt6arGSBv0WpkX2\nf0Ks4LqSQvfo7f9Poca