u/52195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcollina","id":52195,"login":"mcollina","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/62fe5733b3e798d166aa42eb0525fa910dbf3022/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-29T14:01:55Z","email":"hello@matteocollina.com","name":"Matteo Collina"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-29T14:01:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(runtime): log the management API using the runtime logger (#5025)\n\n* feat(runtime): log the management API using the runtime logger\n\nThe management API was created without any logger, so none of its requests\n- nor the log lines already present in its handlers - were ever emitted.\n\nThe management API is now created with the runtime logger. Since it is\nstarted before the logger is created, its creation has been moved after it.\n\nFrequently polled endpoints (status, metadata, config, env, applications,\nmetrics, the live streams and the proxy) are registered with a \"warn\" log\nlevel so that a polling client does not flood the runtime logs, the same\nway the Prometheus server does.\n\nThe management API is closed only after the runtime has been closed, so\nthat the POST /stop endpoint can reply. By then the runtime logger has been\ndestroyed and writing to its destination throws, therefore the logger is\nresolved on each call rather than captured: logging becomes a no-op as soon\nas the runtime replaces its logger with the abstract one.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5[1m]\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n* fix(runtime): avoid management API listen log breaking startup detection\n\nFastify logs listen() at info; for the management API that surfaces a\nprivate unix socket/pipe and was matched by helpers looking for the first\n\"listening at\" message, causing early returns before apps were ready.\n\nDowngrade the management API listen log to debug and harden test helpers\nto only accept HTTP(S) application URLs.\n\nAssisted-by: pi:grok-4.5\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","tree":{"sha":"2e2c80674d4666b7f3d43d100691ea69a2275177","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/trees/2e2c80674d4666b7f3d43d100691ea69a2275177"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/commits/62fe5733b3e798d166aa42eb0525fa910dbf3022","verification":{"payload":"tree 2e2c80674d4666b7f3d43d100691ea69a2275177\nparent 928403936d2608bb0e3825a1fac55f7279aca387\nauthor Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com> 1785333715 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785333715 -0700\n\nfeat(runtime): log the management API using the runtime logger (#5025)\n\n* feat(runtime): log the management API using the runtime logger\n\nThe management API was created without any logger, so none of its requests\n- nor the log lines already present in its handlers - were ever emitted.\n\nThe management API is now created with the runtime logger. Since it is\nstarted before the logger is created, its creation has been moved after it.\n\nFrequently polled endpoints (status, metadata, config, env, applications,\nmetrics, the live streams and the proxy) are registered with a \"warn\" log\nlevel so that a polling client does not flood the runtime logs, the same\nway the Prometheus server does.\n\nThe management API is closed only after the runtime has been closed, so\nthat the POST /stop endpoint can reply. By then the runtime logger has been\ndestroyed and writing to its destination throws, therefore the logger is\nresolved on each call rather than captured: logging becomes a no-op as soon\nas the runtime replaces its logger with the abstract one.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5[1m]\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n* fix(runtime): avoid management API listen log breaking startup detection\n\nFastify logs listen() at info; for the management API that surfaces a\nprivate unix socket/pipe and was matched by helpers looking for the first\n\"listening at\" message, causing early returns before apps were ready.\n\nDowngrade the management API listen log to debug and harden test helpers\nto only accept HTTP(S) application URLs.\n\nAssisted-by: pi:grok-4.5\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqagfTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArrMQAGu4FHpmv3Tv84yFGyzpfUCs\npFaExeQpp+pOQObW5fsQARR5C3q7+rl19yNJCZOXhQZqUUSk1XR1g5YJaASQhpVP\nU8HpYBrGzZilNl9zdxh6DtmN4E5bPLgpv5qV0qBwwsoXXknOBAkEiCcZZWyxBqL4\nYBO1X/OCcztVm5KR3vX3B17IdFPRc9dL4Z8mutUYfYLSzpE+zUvrD6m4qcY4oBUH\nGnWEA8vM/KSI8axIGSAXyDDnF5CdrCb0Py61BVkliA8tNTxVXtYqJvVkiVKBr/F3\n7Lnh8LqQ4mpb0pBhpiTsXS963VCmUm6gBTFmt91OER/3ccMcryFDnR/4lj5nTGYO\n9m1lAIlWrRJ1kqM8taOdhN6X0j9Pfl/DPcFrIp5b0uVIqfhyiPbj6cEwG6oczUEN\nqWJMqSF8/Ku8OmHC6+8PRVZv9MviJ2fReKOwYyuojnFhSP/PUf8c0092rD6iAtz9\n2C4yTV8FV+WiQQ/xHqgYHDnU6J2E+iW5pcROwLtApafD9HsKKTzlrfD+gRrjk8gp\nBKp4PlUeQDQWQ0uhWqeTEtXY39tTJyepkL1vt4BZCH2DuoGfLiNuS1r6XhV6kOgh\naK50ldgWjPlNFt7bBtuzqjApKUzE