tps://api.github.com/users/mcollina/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/platformatic/platformatic/commit/928403936d2608bb0e3825a1fac55f7279aca387","node_id":"C_kwDOIC2I7NoAKDkyODQwMzkzNmQyNjA4YmIwZTM4MjVhMWZhYzU1ZjcyNzlhY2EzODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/platformatic/platformatic/commit/78f77381dc00e955265362a4a248b35244ec8e57","sha":"78f77381dc00e955265362a4a248b35244ec8e57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/78f77381dc00e955265362a4a248b35244ec8e57"}],"sha":"928403936d2608bb0e3825a1fac55f7279aca387","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/928403936d2608bb0e3825a1fac55f7279aca387"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcollina","id":52195,"login":"mcollina","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/78f77381dc00e955265362a4a248b35244ec8e57/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T18:01:22Z","email":"hello@matteocollina.com","name":"Matteo Collina"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T18:01:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(runtime): add typed worker lifecycle events for extensions (#5032)\n\n* feat(runtime): add typed worker lifecycle events for extensions\n\nThe supabase/storage pprof runtime-extension.ts defines interfaces\nfor ''application:worker:started'', ''application:worker:exited'',\n''application:worker:profile:captured'', and\n''application:worker:health:metrics'' events that are emitted by the\nRuntime class but were missing from the TypeScript declarations.\n\nAdd WorkerLifecycleEvent, ProfileCapturedEvent, RuntimeHealthSignal,\nand HealthMetricsEvent interfaces, plus typed on/off overloads on the\nRuntime class so extensions can register typed listeners.\n\nAssisted-by: pi\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n* fixup\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n* fix(runtime): address review on worker lifecycle event types\n\nAllow HealthMetricsEvent.currentHealth to be null when collection fails,\nand keep catch-all on/off overloads so other EventEmitter events remain\nusable for TypeScript consumers.\n\nAssisted-by: Grok:grok-4.5\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n* fix(runtime): tighten ProfileCapturedEvent and currentHealth types\n\nNarrow profile type to ''cpu'' | ''heap'' and type currentHealth as\n{ elu, heapUsed?, heapTotal? } | null per review feedback.\n\nAssisted-by: pi:grok-4.5\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","tree":{"sha":"9abf5954483afa676b3dcdd8763dba494ee8fc89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/trees/9abf5954483afa676b3dcdd8763dba494ee8fc89"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/commits/78f77381dc00e955265362a4a248b35244ec8e57","verification":{"payload":"tree 9abf5954483afa676b3dcdd8763dba494ee8fc89\nparent ab642f3bfcb43afec04a3a2d4dae2319654dfc07\nauthor Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com> 1785261682 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785261682 +0100\n\nfeat(runtime): add typed worker lifecycle events for extensions (#5032)\n\n* feat(runtime): add typed worker lifecycle events for extensions\n\nThe supabase/storage pprof runtime-extension.ts defines interfaces\nfor ''application:worker:started'', ''application:worker:exited'',\n''application:worker:profile:captured'', and\n''application:worker:health:metrics'' events that are emitted by the\nRuntime class but were missing from the TypeScript declarations.\n\nAdd WorkerLifecycleEvent, ProfileCapturedEvent, RuntimeHealthSignal,\nand HealthMetricsEvent interfaces, plus typed on/off overloads on the\nRuntime class so extensions can register typed listeners.\n\nAssisted-by: pi\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n* fixup\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n* fix(runtime): address review on worker lifecycle event types\n\nAllow HealthMetricsEvent.currentHealth to be null when collection fails,\nand keep catch-all on/off overloads so other EventEmitter events remain\nusable for TypeScript consumers.\n\nAssisted-by: Grok:grok-4.5\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n* fix(runtime): tighten ProfileCapturedEvent and currentHealth types\n\nNarrow profile type to ''cpu'' | ''heap'' and type currentHealth as\n{ elu, heapUsed?, heapTotal? } | null per review feedback.\n\nAssisted-by: pi:grok-4.5\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaO5yCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAL60QAI5L2+FHhKug2ptAPQ6gk0dO\nerFbdNRscJ93RhJ7xHm9EOA8EekLFmq6Tw