ab642f3bfcb43afec04a3a2d4dae2319654dfc07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/ab642f3bfcb43afec04a3a2d4dae2319654dfc07"}],"sha":"78f77381dc00e955265362a4a248b35244ec8e57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/78f77381dc00e955265362a4a248b35244ec8e57"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcollina","id":52195,"login":"mcollina","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/ab642f3bfcb43afec04a3a2d4dae2319654dfc07/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T15:13:24Z","email":"hello@matteocollina.com","name":"Matteo Collina"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T15:13:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: complete Phase 5 — applications terminology and capability coverage (#5039)\n\n* docs: complete Phase 5 terminology and capability coverage\n\nAlign the docs with the terminology the CLI already uses. wattpm says\n''applications'' everywhere, so migrate the legacy runtime config keys in\nexamples (''services'' and ''web'' -> ''applications''), the sidebar labels, and\nthe reference headings for HTTP Application, Database Application and\nGateway. Each migrated example was validated against runtime/schema.json.\nIndustry terms are deliberately untouched: microservices, service discovery,\nservice mesh and references to external services are not names for the units\nrunning inside Watt, and a blanket rename would have mangled them.\n\nAlso fixes a regression from the previous PR, where guides/logging.md still\nshowed autoload path ''services'' after the logger example directory was\nrenamed to applications/, and an ''API Gateway (Composer)'' sidebar label the\nGateway rename missed.\n\nCapability coverage: guides/capabilities.md was missing React Router and\nTanStack, and the framework lists in the overview pages and README named\nfour or five of the ten that ship. Overview.md also claimed integration with\n''React, Vue'', neither of which is a capability.\n\nQuick start verified by executing it against Watt 3.64.0, driving the\ngenerator through PLT_USER_INPUT_HANDLER to capture the real prompts.\nCreation, the generated app, npm start and the gateway route all work as\ndocumented. Three transcript inaccuracies fixed: two missing prompts and a\nhard-coded version that goes stale every release.\n\nDocuments a real bug found while doing so: create-next-app web/next names\nthe workspace package ''next'', which under \"workspaces\": [\"web/*\"] makes\nnode_modules/next a symlink to the application and shadows the Next.js\nframework. Reproduces outside Watt, so it is a naming collision rather than\na runtime bug.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n* docs: document the Turbopack workspace-root fix for Next.js in Watt\n\nDigging into the worker exit left open by the previous commit found a second\nbug, independent of the package name collision. With the collision avoided,\nthe next worker still exited with code 1 and no diagnostic output. Running\nNext''s dev binary directly with stderr captured surfaced the real error the\nruntime was swallowing: Turbopack, the default builder in Next.js 16, infers\na workspace root and cannot resolve next/package.json from the application\ndirectory, because npm workspaces hoists next to the Watt project root.\n\nSetting turbopack.root to the Watt project root fixes it. Verified: before,\nfive consecutive ''exited prematurely with error code 1'' retries; after,\n''Started the worker 0'' plus Ready, and GET / through Watt returns 200 with\n~16KB of rendered Next.js markup. Like the name collision this reproduces\nwith plain ''next dev'' outside Watt, so it is an npm workspace resolution\nproblem rather than a Watt runtime bug.\n\nThe Next.js half of the quick start is now verified end to end.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","tree":{"sha":"b4650aad2d3756b9bb4afbd9ef396a97bd112a07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/trees/b4650aad2d3756b9bb4afbd9ef396a97bd112a07"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/commits/ab642f3bfcb43afec04a3a2d4dae2319654dfc07","verification":{"payload":"tree b4650aad2d3756b9bb4afbd9ef396a97bd112a07\nparent e7efdf23df0a26ea18229cfff83eec03aefd6f8c\nauthor Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com> 1785251604 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785251604 -0700\n\ndocs: complete Phase 5 — applications terminology and capability coverage (#5039)\n\n* docs: complete Phase 5 terminology and capability coverage\n\nAlign the docs with the terminology the CLI already uses. wattpm says\n''applications'' everywhere, so migrate the legacy runtime config keys in\nexamples (''services'' and ''web'' -> ''applications''), the sidebar labels, and\nthe reference headings for HTTP Application, Database Application and\nGateway. Each migrated example was validated against runtime/schema.json.\nIndustry terms are deliberately untouched: microservices, service discovery,\nservice mesh and references to external services are not names for the units\nrunning inside Watt, and a blanket rename would have mangled them.\n\nAlso fixes a regression from the previous PR, where guides/logging.md still\nshowed autoload path ''services'' after the logger example directory was\nrenamed to applications/, and an ''API Gateway (Composer)'' sidebar label the\nGateway rename missed.\n\nCapability coverage: guides/capabilities.md was missing React Router and\nTanStack, and the framework lists in the overview pages and README named\nfour or five of the ten that ship. Overview.md also claimed integration with\n''React, Vue'', neither of which is a capability.\n\nQuick start verified by executing it against Watt 3.64.0, driving the\ngenerator through PLT_USER_INPUT_HANDLER to capture the real prompts.\nCreation, the generated app, npm start and the gateway route all work as\ndocumented. Three transcript inaccuracies fixed: two missing prompts and a\nhard-coded version that goes stale every release.\n\nDocuments a real bug found while doing so: create-next-app web/next names\nthe workspace package ''next'', which under \"workspaces\": [\"web/*\"] makes\nnode_modules/next a symlink to the application and shadows the Next.js\nframework. Reproduces outside Watt, so it is a naming collision rather than\na runtime bug.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n* docs: document the Turbopack workspace-root fix for Next.js in Watt\n\nDigging into the worker exit left open by the previous commit found a second\nbug, independent of the package name collision. With the collision avoided,\nthe next worker still exited with code 1 and no diagnostic output. Running\nNext''s dev binary directly with stderr captured surfaced the real error the\nruntime was swallowing: Turbopack, the default builder in Next.js 16, infers\na workspace root and cannot resolve next/package.json from the application\ndirectory, because npm workspaces hoists next to the Watt project root.\n\nSetting turbopack.root to the Watt project root fixes it. Verified: before,\nfive consecutive ''exited prematurely with error code 1'' retries; after,\n''Started the worker 0'' plus Ready, and GET / through Watt returns 200 with\n~16KB of rendered Next.js markup. Like the name collision this reproduces\nwith plain ''next dev'' outside Watt, so it is an npm workspace resolution\nproblem rather than a Watt runtime bug.\n\nThe Next.js half of the quick start is now verified end to end.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaMcUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEbQQADpRA95Sojee3oo9EgnskubH\nxJJROhOGyxOYgr68WsUVUl0zRQ8ERaNBDR25seMfyIEzsFmLTPLlD4tN/Xg5fYOp\neVOjHnChUUA01+obr9t34Uuk+cCO7tmKmqzvK8KinsEnXXPPmOG4tgEJQhboaJT2\nQdpHnpG1hj8AeK1wDBOmd86K/2v2NwS94i2m0SuMsDqHeU2eDVqL1gm0qVd0PTwK\ntE/FfE77vskmX9gCV1otfqH9BlUc1ITUkrAljU9AmEFK7ONzse9fU22qrL1ZVudR\n84qkpXFQce+LiJ3nOaZjxnyTZynNBuEwFmJtgZ+oaiWqSB0lupsmKbd/FR/JlIW5\npd5pF9o6/TMsBOMeUlt7e+0lBZeK6S1ODbj2+G6DRStAQSu0KxeVXRmlDDcOy/sc\n01j5Ml3JnzqWhuakNpLZontemJn7Dqpu37ZIT/KgD/DMV4WvEQjpRwm6L0qnaxFF\nEvU7fYoluI13OMgnfM+0hXXYkfSdXiwyBWe0mby6oCp/tMb0vqchRu/S8s5hr3mX\nOVfQzvlsOHJm3se2/qkeaIUEt3q7hCiKAaNqyco4pSludpM+soeBkE0OKYp5ix0t\n4VAfQftOYNCjJf6ZF9oxCoVbLacDS6ZfgWyWUB2trvBA5hEEbyASxIUJQWKou61s\nRhdNMExzTMlIaYAPSOvG\n=5qxX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-28T15:13:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/platformatic/platformatic/commit/ab642f3bfcb43afec04a3a2d4dae2319654dfc07","node_id":"C_kwDOIC2I7NoAKGFiNjQyZjNiZmNiNDNhZmVjMDRhM2EyZDRkYWUyMzE5NjU0ZGZjMDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/platformatic/platformatic/commit/e7efdf23df0a26ea18229cfff83eec03aefd6f8c","sha":"e7efdf23df0a26ea18229cfff83eec03aefd6f8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/e7efdf23df0a26ea18229cfff83eec03aefd6f8c"}],"sha":"ab642f3bfcb43afec04a3a2d4dae2319654dfc07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/ab642f3bfcb43afec04a3a2d4dae2319654dfc07"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mcollina","id":52195,"login":"mcollina","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcollina","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/commits/e7efdf23df0a26ea18229cfff83eec03aefd6f8c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T14:20:02Z","email":"hello@matteocollina.com","name":"Matteo Collina"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T14:20:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(runtime): resolve extension setup through faux ESM and named setup exports (#5037)\n\nExtensions were loaded by reading only the `default` property of the imported\nmodule namespace. That breaks for the modules transpilers and bundlers emit:\nthey put the real exports on `module.exports` next to an `__esModule` marker,\nand Node''s CJS interop exposes the whole `module.exports` object as the ESM\ndefault export. The setup function is therefore one level deeper, at\n`.default.default`, and the runtime rejected the extension with\nPLT_RUNTIME_INVALID_EXTENSION even though it was well formed.\n\nExtension loading now resolves the setup function through\nresolveExtensionSetup(), which takes the first function among `default`,\n`setup`, `default.default` and `default.setup`. This unwraps the extra interop\nhop and, at the same time, adds support for exporting the setup function as a\nnamed `setup` export, in both plain ESM and faux ESM form.\n\nThe default export keeps precedence over a named `setup` export, so an\nextension that happens to expose both is unaffected. The\nPLT_RUNTIME_INVALID_EXTENSION message now names both accepted shapes, and the\nconfiguration reference documents the resolution order and the failure mode.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","tree":{"sha":"cc0a82665fe5e4d41fd85ff95d37a4e5c784bd81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/trees/cc0a82665fe5e4d41fd85ff95d37a4e5c784bd81"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platformatic/platformatic/git/commits/e7efdf23df0a26ea18229cfff83eec03aefd6f8c","verification":{"payload":"tree cc0a82665fe5e4d41fd85ff95d37a4e5c784bd81\nparent c6d7f9673aa2dba4bdd1110db527f55c0aa70a8e\nauthor Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com> 1785248402 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785248402 -0700\n\nfeat(runtime): resolve extension setup through faux ESM and named setup exports (#5037)\n\nExtensions were loaded by reading only the `default` property of the imported\nmodule namespace. That breaks for the modules transpilers and bundlers emit:\nthey put the real exports on `module.exports` next to an `__esModule` marker,\nand Node''s CJS interop exposes the whole `module.exports` object as the ESM\ndefault export. The setup function is therefore one level deeper, at\n`.default.default`, and the runtime rejected the extension with\nPLT_RUNTIME_INVALID_EXTENSION even though it was well formed.\n\nExtension loading now resolves the setup function through\nresolveExtensionSetup(), which takes the first function among `default`,\n`setup`, `default.default` and `default.setup`. This unwraps the extra interop\nhop and, at the same time, adds support for exporting the setup function as a\nnamed `setup` export, in both plain ESM and faux ESM form.\n\nThe default export keeps precedence over a named `setup` export, so an\nextension that happens to expose both is unaffected. The\nPLT_RUNTIME_INVALID_EXTENSION message now names both accepted shapes, and the\nconfiguration reference documents the resolution order and the failure mode.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5\n\nSigned-off-by: Matteo Collina <hello@matteocollina.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaLqSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARG8QAIv9oEXQ5jx9+Kmxoeatg8+u\n7vs2Q7Wq/4Bp1DwRfsmF34uhxXRiNaVKy5uynX3XyLRvPRLr4RyUvsvFjy5J6fsq\n3km2lusBQdPA6Rxzg+JM